From: WPE4YDPv2 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: allow bypassing intermediate incoming-track sync

Incoming WebRTC samples are handed from an intermediate fakesink to the
RealtimeIncomingSource and then pushed into the MediaStream playback pipeline.
The final playback pipeline already performs clock synchronization.

Some cloud gaming servers expose RTP timestamps far ahead of the local
pipeline running time. Synchronizing the intermediate fakesink to those
timestamps blocks its queue after a few decoded frames, even though RTP
packets continue to arrive.

Keep the upstream behavior by default and add an explicit runtime switch for
the embedded receiver. This keeps the experiment independently reversible.

---
 .../gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp       | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp
@@ -102,8 +102,12 @@ void GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor::configure(ThreadSafeWeakPtr<GStreamerMedi
     if (!m_sdpMsIdAndTrackId.second.isEmpty())
         m_data.trackId = m_sdpMsIdAndTrackId.second;
 
+    bool synchronizeIncomingSamples = g_strcmp0(g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_WEBRTC_DISABLE_INCOMING_SYNC"), "1");
     m_sink = gst_element_factory_make("fakesink", "sink");
-    g_object_set(m_sink.get(), "sync", TRUE, "enable-last-sample", FALSE, "qos", TRUE, nullptr);
+    g_object_set(m_sink.get(), "sync", synchronizeIncomingSamples, "enable-last-sample", FALSE, "qos", TRUE, nullptr);
+    GST_INFO_OBJECT(m_sink.get(), "Intermediate incoming-track clock synchronization: %s",
+        synchronizeIncomingSamples ? "enabled" : "disabled");
+
     auto queue = gst_element_factory_make("queue", "queue");
 
     auto trackProcessor = incomingTrackProcessor();
